{"name":"Corkboard","hex":"#9d805d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"corkboard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of cork-board."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corkboard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bulletin board","blocks":[{"text":"A bulletin board is a surface intended for the posting of messages, for example public ones may advertise items wanted or for sale, announce events, or provide information. Bulletin boards are often made of a material such as cork to facilitate addition and removal of messages, as well as a writing surface such as whiteboard or blackboard. A bulletin board which combines a pinboard (corkboard) and writing surface is known as a combination bulletin board. Bulletin boards can also be entirely in the digital domain and placed on computer networks so people can leave and erase messages for other people to read and see, as in a bulletin board system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Infinite-corridor-bboard.jpeg/330px-Infinite-corridor-bboard.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulletin_board"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg/500px-Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg/1280px-Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg/500px-Drawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fanciful drawing of a general store by Marguerite Martyn in the St. Louis Post-Dispatch of October 21, 1906. A man at right reads a notice of a revival service on a bulletin board.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrawing_of_a_country_store_by_Marguerite_Martyn.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Brown University 1792 engraving","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg/500px-Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg","ratio":1.5094170403587444,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg","share":0.143125},{"title":"Post Office High Road Postbox ^ Notice Board - geograph.org.uk - 4985532","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Post_Office_High_Road_Postbox_%5E_Notice_Board_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4985532.jpg/500px-Post_Office_High_Road_Postbox_%5E_Notice_Board_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4985532.jpg","ratio":0.7519511367492365,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Post_Office_High_Road_Postbox_%5E_Notice_Board_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4985532.jpg","share":0.135625},{"title":"Chapin House, Brown University","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Chapin_House%2C_Brown_University.jpg/500px-Chapin_House%2C_Brown_University.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chapin_House,_Brown_University.jpg","share":0.121875},{"title":"Sèvres - Magot - Pajou, buste de Madame du Barry 08","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou%2C_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg/500px-S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou%2C_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%A8vres_-_Magot_-_Pajou,_buste_de_Madame_du_Barry_08.jpg","share":0.11875},{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russ